  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "Rinse brisket and tripe in water and then place into a large stockpot. Add water to cover completely (About 2 quarts). Bring to a boil over high heat, reduce heat to low, and add cinnamon, black pepper, salt, and ginger. Simmer until tender, 2 to 2 1/2 hours. Remove from heat and allow brisket and tripe to cool in broth.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, make the chile sauce. Combine Sichuan peppercorns, sesame paste, soy sauce, and chile oil. Set aside.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "primary_message": "When the brisket and tripe have cooled down, remove from the broth and cut on a bias into 0.5-cm slices. Add 1/4 cup beef broth to chile-sesame mixture and stir to combine. Dress the brisket and tripe liberally in the sauce, tossing to coat all the slices. Add the chopped cilantro and serve at room temperature. Leftovers may be kept in the refrigerator for 1-2 days.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
